Windows driver helper source and build material

libwdi is licensed under LGPL version 3 or later. Its complete source
and original copyright notices are in the accompanying source archive.
The supplied patches select the built-in WinUSB driver on Windows 10/11
and make embedded resource timestamps honor SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH.
The build recipe applies them to a fresh source tree.

On Linux, install GCC and patch. Verify the SHA-256 digests in downloads.json and
download the pinned llvm_mingw input. Extract the toolchain and supplied
libwdi archives, then run:

python3 build.py --toolchain <llvm-mingw-directory> \
  --source <libwdi-directory> \
  --source-date-epoch $SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH --output <wdi-simple.exe>

The build runs only the native resource embedder. It does not execute
Windows programs or install a driver on the build host.
